# The voices' rows in the launcher's Accessibility category: Your voice a
# step Right and back, Your voice volume a step down and back, Preview your
# voice and Preview opponents' voice pressed with Enter. Each step on a
# Voice or Volume row logs the saved value and the reader's new value, then
# a moment later the sample in that voice and its "plays" line; Preview
# plays at once. With the screen reader muted the voices still render and
# play, into SDL's dummy driver. Expects the voices ready by the time the
# category opens, and at least two voices installed. The run's a11y.ini
# starts from the defaults. Run in launcher mode, with accessibility on but
# muted, and with Steering and Cues left to the run's a11y.ini, so no row
# shows "(environment)" (as run_level.py runs it):
#   MELEE_A11Y_STEER= MELEE_A11Y_CUES= python tools/a11y/drive.py --launcher --muted tools/a11y/launcher_voices.drive
# run_level.py also counts the samples: five in your voice and one in the
# opponents' voice, one for each settled step and one for each Preview.

wait '"Melee launcher\. Ready to play'
key Down Down Down
wait '"Settings, button\. '
key Return
wait '"Settings\. Graphics\. '
key Down Down Down Down Down
wait '"Accessibility\. Speech, steering and the audio cues of Non-Visual Melee\."$'
key Right
wait '"Accessibility, On, Left and right to change\. '

# Your voice, right after Speech, the voice in use not pinned.
key Down Down
wait '"Your voice, (?P<yours>[^",]+)(, [^"]+)?, Left and right to change\. The Windows voice that says what happens to you in a match\."$'

# A step Right: the next voice, saved by its display name, said alone, and a
# moment later its sample; then Left back to the voice the run started on.
key Right
wait '\[a11y\] accessibility settings: saved your_voice\.voice = (?P<next>[^,]+)$'
wait '\[a11y\] speak \w+ \(muted\): "%next%(, [^"]+)?"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours: "Your voice"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours plays: "Your voice" \(rendered in \d+ ms, \d+ ms after it was said\)$'
ini '^your_voice\.voice = %next%$'
key Left
wait '\[a11y\] accessibility settings: saved your_voice\.voice = %yours%$'
wait '\[a11y\] speak \w+ \(muted\): "%yours%(, [^"]+)?"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours: "Your voice"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours plays: "Your voice" '
ini '^your_voice\.voice = %yours%$'

# Your voice volume a step down and back up, each with its sample.
key Down Down
wait '"Your voice volume, slider, 100%\. Left and right to adjust\. The loudness of your voice, under the master volume\."$'
key Left
wait '\[a11y\] accessibility settings: saved your_voice\.volume = 95$'
wait '"95%"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours: "Your voice"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours plays: "Your voice" '
ini '^your_voice\.volume = 95$'
key Right
wait '\[a11y\] accessibility settings: saved your_voice\.volume = 100$'
wait '"100%"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours: "Your voice"$'
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours plays: "Your voice" '
ini '^your_voice\.volume = 100$'

# Preview your voice: Enter plays the sample at once.
key Down
wait '"Preview your voice: Play, button\. Says "Your voice" in your voice, at its rate and volume\."$'
key Return
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours: "Your voice"$' 0.3
wait '\[a11y\] voice yours plays: "Your voice" '

# Preview opponents' voice, past the opponents' other three rows.
key Down Down Down Down
wait "\"Preview opponents' voice: Play, button\. Says \"Opponents' voice\" in the opponents' voice, at its rate and volume\.\"$"
key Return
wait "\[a11y\] voice opponents: \"Opponents' voice\"$" 0.3
wait "\[a11y\] voice opponents plays: \"Opponents' voice\" "

# Escape twice: the category, then Home.
key Escape
wait '"Accessibility\. Speech, steering '
key Escape
wait '"Settings, button\. '
